# Research Rules: Session Filter (H-S1)

Status: DRAFT. Becomes binding only when committed. After commit, only the Run Log (section 9) may change.

Related: Z hypothesis is PARKED (unproven, not retired). Its rules document is separate and unchanged.

---

## 1. Question (one only)

Do trades from the frozen setup that are *signalled* during the London/NY overlap have a higher mean R than trades signalled outside it?

This is one question. No other filters, symbols, exits or fill modes are tested under this document.

## 2. Hypothesis

H-S1: mean R (in-window) minus mean R (out-of-window) is greater than 0.

Reason to believe it (stated before testing): the overlap has the most liquidity and the most stop runs, which is when a sweep-and-reverse setup should work best.

## 3. Data

- **Dev data** (80,000 candles, 2025-08-20 to 2026-10-06): used up. Allowed uses: trade counts, SD of R, and sanity checks. Looking at the in-window vs out-of-window effect on dev data is allowed only as *exploratory*, must be written in the Run Log, and does not count toward the decision.
- **Holdout data**: new, non-overlapping data never used for any development. Priority: gold history before 2025-08-20 or after 2026-10-06; second choice: a basket of other symbols (each symbol is a separate test, pooled only if section 6 says so).
- The holdout file is committed before it is run. Record: file name, row count, git commit hash of these rules.

## 4. Frozen setup (no edits after the freeze)

- Fill mode: market on close (touch, then fill at next bar's open). Touch fill is NOT used (it books unachievable fills).
- No MTF gate, no ATR widening.
- Exit: structural 15M swing target, minimum 1.5R. *(OPEN: see section 10, Q2.)*
- Cost: 0.5 price units round trip, fixed, for the decision. Cost 1.0 reported as sensitivity only.
- Trade pool: ALL trades from the frozen setup, regardless of Z/A/B/X tag.
- Frozen files: strategy/backtest.py, signals.py, retest_engine.py, structure_targets.py, swings.py, zones.py, liquidity.py, mtf_structure.py, dashboard/mtf_context.py, requirements.txt, and every tool used for this test.
- Freeze starts when the holdout file is committed.

## 5. Definition of "in-window"

- Timestamps are true UTC (the data check shows daily reopen moving 22:00 / 23:00 with US daylight saving, which is what UTC data of a CME-linked market looks like).
- In-window = trade signal time between **13:00 and 17:00 UTC**, Monday to Friday.
- The window is fixed in UTC and is not adjusted for daylight saving. Real overlap shifts by one hour for part of the year; that is accepted as noise.
- The window is chosen now and not tuned. If it is changed after any result is seen, the test is void.

## 6. Analysis (the one number)

- One tool, one run, one configuration.
- De-duplication: if two trades open on the same calendar day in the same direction, keep the first only.
- Estimate: OLS of net R on an in-window dummy, with standard errors clustered by calendar day.
- Read only: the in-window coefficient, its cluster-robust SE, and the 80% confidence interval.
- Pooling: gold holdout is its own test. Other symbols are separate tests. They are pooled into one decision only if all are run under identical rules and the pooled design is stated in the Run Log before any of them is run.

## 7. Decision rule (single decision, preset size)

- **Minimum sample:** the decision is made once, when the smaller group (in or out) reaches the trade count N* from section 8. No peeking before that. No per-holdout verdicts.
- **Smallest worthwhile effect (SWE):** +0.20R.
- **PASS:** coefficient > 0 and the lower end of the 80% CI is above 0.
- **RULED OUT:** the upper end of the 80% CI is below +0.20R. Only then is H-S1 set aside.
- **INCONCLUSIVE:** anything else. This is not a failure and not a pass; it means more data is needed.
- "Two fails in a row" is NOT used.

## 8. Sample size (power calculation)

Rough numbers, to be recomputed from the real SD of R on dev data before the freeze:

- Assume SD of R about 1.5.
- To detect 0.30R difference with 80% power (one-sided 5%): about 310 trades per group.
- To detect 0.20R: about 700 per group.
- N* is set to the number the final calculation gives. It is written here before commit: **N* = ____ per group.**

**Feasibility warning:** the CI log shows about 34 closed trades in roughly 6 months under the gated market-on-close setup. Even if the ungated pool is several times larger, a few hundred trades per group is many years on gold alone. If the dev-data trade rate says N* cannot be reached in a reasonable time, this test must be run on a basket of symbols or the question must be dropped. Fill in the ungated trade rate here: **trades per year (ungated, dev data) = ____.**

